1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:45,980
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:48,400
=Episode 12=

4
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:07,310
Your Majesty.

5
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,310
I didn't know.

6
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:10,340
I was only concerned for your health.

7
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,030
Effective today, Consort Chen

8
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:22,220
is confined to her quarters
to pray for me and copy sutras.

9
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:24,300
You may leave only after

10
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:25,670
completing ten volumes.

11
00:01:25,990 --> 00:01:26,780
Your Majesty.

12
00:01:28,990 --> 00:01:30,470
Weren't you worried about me?

13
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:35,670
Yes.

14
00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:37,390
I'll go right away.

15
00:01:55,910 --> 00:01:56,580
Su.

16
00:02:04,990 --> 00:02:06,340
Now that the truth is clear,

17
00:02:07,030 --> 00:02:07,910
I'll take my leave.

18
00:02:15,110 --> 00:02:16,110
Let go of me!

19
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:17,510
Let go of me!

20
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:20,460
I'm sorry.

21
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:22,550
Su.

22
00:02:23,390 --> 00:02:24,510
Why didn't you tell me?

23
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:31,670
If my sleepless nights

24
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,700
can help Your Majesty sleep soundly,

25
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:36,140
then such a small sacrifice

26
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:37,740
is hardly worth mentioning.

27
00:02:39,110 --> 00:02:40,420
You carry the burdens of the realm

28
00:02:40,830 --> 00:02:41,830
and worry for your people.

29
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,550
If I can ease your burden,

30
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:46,990
I'd gladly bear any hardship.

31
00:02:55,390 --> 00:02:56,420
You treated me

32
00:02:56,860 --> 00:02:58,180
at the cost of your own health.

33
00:03:00,580 --> 00:03:01,270
You deserve a reward.

34
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,860
I'll grant you the rank of Noble Lady.

35
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:07,110
We'll choose an auspicious day
for you to enter the palace.

36
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:09,790
Stay by my side forever.

37
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:11,230
Will you?

38
00:03:15,270 --> 00:03:16,390
I'm deeply grateful, Your Majesty.

39
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:18,790
But my station is too low.

40
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:20,950
I fear you'd give people reason to talk.

41
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:23,230
I'd rather leave the capital,

42
00:03:23,950 --> 00:03:25,830
even as a traveling healer.

43
00:03:28,110 --> 00:03:29,350
Do you blame me?

44
00:03:32,550 --> 00:03:34,020
I'm a healer by trade.

45
00:03:34,550 --> 00:03:38,180
I prefer treating people
out in the countryside.

46
00:03:39,790 --> 00:03:42,110
Palace life may not suit me.

47
00:03:51,670 --> 00:03:54,510
I know you care about those
who can't afford treatment.

48
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:57,390
I can establish

49
00:03:57,740 --> 00:03:58,860
a Charity Clinic in your name

50
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:01,620
outside the palace.

51
00:04:02,990 --> 00:04:03,790
Would that

52
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:05,790
convince you to stay by my side?

53
00:04:12,110 --> 00:04:13,270
Are you going to defy my order?

54
00:04:16,510 --> 00:04:17,420
I wouldn't dare.

55
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:21,700
I'm deeply grateful, Your Majesty.

56
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:23,380
Then...

57
00:04:23,710 --> 00:04:24,590
I'll take my leave.

58
00:04:35,350 --> 00:04:35,940
Your Majesty.

59
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:37,350
Didn't you already know

60
00:04:37,590 --> 00:04:38,860
the sachet was harmless?

61
00:04:39,110 --> 00:04:40,670
I did know all along.

62
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:45,030
Your Majesty.

63
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:46,620
The imperial physician examined it.

64
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:47,790
The pillow contains

65
00:04:48,150 --> 00:04:50,300
asarum and raw pinellia,

66
00:04:50,470 --> 00:04:51,820
but they've been properly processed
to counteract each other's toxicity.

67
00:04:52,150 --> 00:04:54,180
They aid sleep without causing harm.

68
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:56,790
Don't let this get out.

69
00:04:56,910 --> 00:04:57,550
You may go.

70
00:04:58,590 --> 00:04:59,260
Yes.

71
00:05:00,670 --> 00:05:02,230
Consort Chen still has

72
00:05:03,590 --> 00:05:05,060
Zhang Heng backing her.

73
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:06,860
This was the only way

74
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:09,670
to bring the woman I love
into the palace.

75
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:13,910
(By the Mandate of Heaven,
the Emperor decrees:)

76
00:05:14,030 --> 00:05:15,940
(Su Cao is gentle and virtuous.)

77
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,180
(She has won my favor.)

78
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:18,820
(She is hereby made a Noble Lady.)

79
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:20,710
(She is granted the title Hui.)

80
00:05:21,030 --> 00:05:22,710
(Buddhist Scripture)
(Granted Residence: Jiyun Pavilion.)

81
00:05:22,710 --> 00:05:24,300
(Thus decreed.)

82
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:29,820
Bad news!

83
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:31,300
Bad news, Your Highness!

84
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,110
Your Highness, it's terrible!

85
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:36,790
What is it?

86
00:05:37,550 --> 00:05:38,420
That village woman...

87
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:40,150
was made a Noble Lady.

88
00:05:45,150 --> 00:05:45,990
Impossible.

89
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:48,030
That's impossible!

90
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:53,550
It took me three years

91
00:05:53,710 --> 00:05:55,060
just to become a Noble Lady.

92
00:05:55,670 --> 00:05:56,940
That wretch

93
00:05:57,420 --> 00:05:59,300
only used a few seductive tricks,

94
00:06:00,030 --> 00:06:01,620
and rose so high overnight!

95
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:03,230
Why should she?

96
00:06:04,260 --> 00:06:05,260
Why should she?

97
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,810
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

98
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:31,010
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

99
00:06:31,950 --> 00:06:34,250
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

100
00:06:34,570 --> 00:06:36,320
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

101
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:40,220
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

102
00:06:41,050 --> 00:06:44,210
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

103
00:06:45,420 --> 00:06:48,570
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

104
00:06:49,490 --> 00:06:51,820
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

105
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:54,000
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

106
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:57,250
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

107
00:06:58,250 --> 00:07:01,400
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

108
00:07:02,990 --> 00:07:06,450
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

109
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:09,280
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

110
00:07:10,030 --> 00:07:13,630
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

111
00:07:15,090 --> 00:07:18,220
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

112
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:23,450
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

113
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:31,800
♪The past has faded away♪

114
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:35,800
♪The past has faded away♪
